WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:15.292
When Beth opened her eyes her first thought was that she had died and gone to heaven.

2
00:00:15.293 --> 00:00:21.817
Then she decided she was still dreaming because Mother was standing over her, smiling and calling her name.

3
00:00:21.818 --> 00:00:26.701
"No, it can't be real," Beth said to herself.

4
00:00:26.702 --> 00:00:31.502
"Mother is with Father. She can't be here with me."

5
00:00:31.503 --> 00:00:36.246
"Hello, my darling girl," Mother said, stroking her cheek.

6
00:00:36.247 --> 00:00:44.049
Beth tried to speak but didn't have the strength to move her lips, so instead she made a tiny sound in her throat.

7
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:50.759
"I'm here, Beth," Mother said, "and so is Jo. She's never left your bedside."

8
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.932
Seeing Jo's weary face, Beth knew she was no longer dreaming.

9
00:00:55.933 --> 00:01:01.377
Holding out a weak hand to Jo, Beth parted her lips and whispered her sister's name.

10
00:01:01.378 --> 00:01:06.666
Grasping her hand, Jo fell to her knees and cried tears of joy and relief.

11
00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:10.592
News of Beth's recovery certainly brightened everyone's day.

12
00:01:10.593 --> 00:01:18.523
Jo, in particular, found herself smiling for no reason and doing out-of-the-ordinary things like singing aloud.

13
00:01:18.524 --> 00:01:24.115
"When should we get Amy?" Meg asked as she and Jo helped Hannah prepare dinner that evening.

14
00:01:24.116 --> 00:01:31.837
Meg seemed to be in an unusually cheerful mood herself, with flushed cheeks and sparkling eyes that gave her face a glow.

15
00:01:31.838 --> 00:01:35.967
"I'll go tomorrow morning. Maybe I'll ask Laurie to come with me,"

16
00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:42.176
said Jo, chopping some carrots and throwing them into the large pot where a special soup was boiling for Beth.

17
00:01:42.177 --> 00:01:46.947
Meg nodded dreamily as she crushed some peppers and added them to the soup.

18
00:01:46.948 --> 00:01:50.687
"You're awfully merry today," teased Jo.

19
00:01:50.688 --> 00:01:55.171
Meg turned away but replied, "I'm happy that Beth is better."

20
00:01:55.172 --> 00:01:58.619
"We all are, but there's something else.

21
00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:03.542
Come, Meg, what are you hiding?" Jo persisted.

22
00:02:03.543 --> 00:02:13.568
Meg looked over her shoulder to make sure that Hannah was out of earshot, then, pulling Jo to a corner, she pulled out a note from her apron pocket.

23
00:02:13.569 --> 00:02:16.754
"What's this?" whispered Jo, opening the note.

24
00:02:16.755 --> 00:02:26.129
"Just read it, but promise me you won't say a word to Mother or anyone else. It's for your eyes only," said Meg in a hushed voice.

25
00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:33.032
As Jo read the short message, her head began to spin and she felt a hot wave of anger rising up.

26
00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:39.116
It was from John Brookes, and the man was confessing his love for Meg.

27
00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:44.802
"You're too young!" were Jo's first words, practically throwing the note back to Meg.

28
00:02:44.803 --> 00:02:48.575
"I'm almost 18," Meg replied in a huff.

29
00:02:48.576 --> 00:02:51.865
"You just turned 17!" Jo argued.

30
00:02:51.866 --> 00:02:58.407
"It doesn't matter. He loves me, Jo," Meg said, brushing aside Jo's concerns.

31
00:02:58.408 --> 00:03:09.514
"I think it's scandalous! He's too old for you and besides, why is he sending you a note like that at a time like this?" Jo nearly yelled.

32
00:03:09.515 --> 00:03:19.249
"I think it's romantic, and I thought you'd be more supportive and happier for me," Meg said in a hurt voice. Then she added, "He's only 24."

33
00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:24.775
"I'm disgusted with Brookes and with you!" Jo growled at her sister.

34
00:03:24.776 --> 00:03:30.745
With that, Jo yanked off her apron, stormed out of the house, and bumped into an incoming visitor.

35
00:03:30.746 --> 00:03:39.791
"Do you think we might have telepathic powers, because I was just coming to see you," Laurie said when he realized who had just bumped into him.

36
00:03:39.792 --> 00:03:44.849
"This is no time to joke, Laurie," said Jo, cracking her knuckles loudly.

37
00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:49.211
"All right, then," said Laurie. "How's our girl doing?"

38
00:03:49.212 --> 00:03:56.420
"Thank you for asking, Beth is much better. Now, my question is: Are you available to help me get Amy tomorrow?"

39
00:03:56.421 --> 00:03:59.398
Jo asked in a very businesslike manner.

40
00:03:59.399 --> 00:04:04.359
"I'm at your service anytime, anywhere," Laurie replied, bowing like a servant.

41
00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:10.250
"Good. We'll leave at 9 a.m. sharp," said Jo, turning around to go back inside.

42
00:04:10.251 --> 00:04:15.864
"Wait! How's your other sister doing?" Laurie asked slyly.

43
00:04:15.865 --> 00:04:22.421
"She's fine. Why?" suddenly Jo noticed something in Laurie's mischievous eyes.

44
00:04:22.422 --> 00:04:29.161
"Theodore Laurence," she said sternly, "is there something you want to tell me?"

45
00:04:29.162 --> 00:04:37.537
Laurie covered his mouth and let out a muffled shout, then he said in a low whisper, "Did she get a note from Brookes?"

46
00:04:37.538 --> 00:04:43.377
Jo narrowed her eyes and answered, "What if she did? What do you know about it?"

47
00:04:43.378 --> 00:04:47.954
Laurie slapped his knee and threw back his head, laughing loudly.

48
00:04:47.955 --> 00:04:54.404
"It was me! I wrote it! Brookes knows nothing about it!" the prankster admitted.

49
00:04:54.405 --> 00:05:02.628
Jo could not believe her ears but worse yet, she could not believe that Laurie would play such a cruel joke on Meg.

50
00:05:02.629 --> 00:05:08.940
"You . . . you . . .," Jo stuttered. She was so angry that she could not even speak.

51
00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:12.394
Instead she kicked him in the shins with all her might.

52
00:05:12.395 --> 00:05:18.731
"Ow! Why did you do that?" Laurie rubbed his sore leg, hopping on the other foot.

53
00:05:18.732 --> 00:05:22.981
"What happens when Meg discovers that this was all a big joke?

54
00:05:22.982 --> 00:05:27.347
How will this affect her self-esteem and pride?" Jo spat at him.

55
00:05:27.348 --> 00:05:32.566
"Brookes is in love with her, like I told you," Laurie said, massaging his leg.

56
00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:36.633
"I'm just helping the progress of this relationship."

57
00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:45.440
"You march in there right now," Jo said, pointing toward her house, "and apologize to Meg for what you did before it's too late!"

58
00:05:45.441 --> 00:05:53.484
"Why are you really upset, Jo? Are you afraid that John is going to take away your precious sister?" Laurie asked.

59
00:05:53.485 --> 00:05:57.780
That question got him another hard kick in the other leg.

60
00:05:57.781 --> 00:06:02.495
"Ow! You're going to cripple me, Josephine March!" wailed Laurie.

61
00:06:02.496 --> 00:06:07.962
"Apologize to my sister, though I won't be surprised if she never speaks to you again.

62
00:06:07.963 --> 00:06:16.827
You'd better do it this instant, or else . . . ," Jo paused to form her words carefully, ". . . or else our friendship ends tonight."

63
00:06:16.828 --> 00:06:24.140
Jo turned her back on Laurie, who was rubbing both shins but staring up at her with a worried expression.

64
00:06:24.141 --> 00:06:27.308
"Do you mean that, Jo?" he asked quietly.

65
00:06:27.309 --> 00:06:31.650
Without looking at him, Jo simply replied, "Yes."

66
00:06:31.651 --> 00:06:38.841
Frightened that Jo would carry out her threat, Laurie immediately went to see Meg and told her of his cruel joke.

67
00:06:38.842 --> 00:06:45.214
Meg, being so sweet and ladylike, forgave Laurie and told him that it was not important.

68
00:06:45.215 --> 00:06:48.735
In her heart, however, she was crushed.

69
00:06:48.736 --> 00:06:52.355
Mother sensed right away how heartbroken Meg was.

70
00:06:52.356 --> 00:06:58.430
"It's going to be fine, darling," Mother comforted Meg as she lovingly stroked her head.

71
00:06:58.431 --> 00:07:04.400
"I thought he loved me. I . . . was so happy," sobbed Meg.

72
00:07:04.401 --> 00:07:07.515
Mother thought for a moment before she spoke.

73
00:07:07.516 --> 00:07:15.029
"Meg, darling, I don't know if I should say this, but both your father and I have grown very fond of John.

74
00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:18.549
He is a wonderful, kind, intelligent man.

75
00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:22.303
One day I'm sure he will make a fine husband."

76
00:07:22.304 --> 00:07:25.953
"But not for me," wailed Meg.

77
00:07:25.954 --> 00:07:33.522
"I wouldn't say that," Mother said hesitantly. "I know for a fact that he thinks highly of you.

78
00:07:33.523 --> 00:07:37.836
He speaks with you in the warmest, most respectful way.

79
00:07:37.837 --> 00:07:44.559
I wonder if perhaps Laurie's joke, bad as it was, may have some truth in it."

80
00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:50.148
Meg sniffed but lifted her head and asked, "Do you think John likes me?"

81
00:07:50.149 --> 00:07:56.522
Mother smiled and replied, "How could he not?"
